WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:03.460
It might be hard to put on a happy face after
hearing these comments.

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:07.339
Actor and comedian Marc Maron, who plays a
character named Ted Marco in the upcoming

00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:11.610
Joker movie, made some head-turning remarks
about Marvel movies, and their fans, during

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.620
a recent interview with Conan O'Brien.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:14.919
"I generally don't like them.

00:00:14.919 --> 00:00:18.330
Because I don't wanna be bullied into seeing
those.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.660
Look, Conan, I'm a grown-up, I'm not seven."

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:25.360
Maron appeared on Conan to promote Netflix's
acclaimed comedy-drama series GLOW, which

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:29.860
recently entered its third season, on which
he stars as the gruff but oddly lovable Sam

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:30.500
Sylvia.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.440
Somewhere in their conversation, the topic
shifted to Avengers: Endgame, given many were

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:38.450
convinced that Maron played the younger Stan
Lee in a cameo appearance and was just being

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:39.920
coy about owning up to it.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:44.420
Maron confirmed that it wasn't him, and admitted
that he has some issues with Marvel movies.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:48.200
He then offered his unfiltered thoughts on
the superhero genre as a whole as well as

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:49.340
the people who enjoy it.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:53.560
"I think those movies are for, you know, grown
male nerd childs."

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:57.880
When the Conan audience began to boo, Maron
addressed them directly and said that they

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:01.320
should accept the criticism, since they're,
quote, "in charge of culture."

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:05.190
He also expressed frustration over the fact
that he has to take extra steps to see the

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:09.610
movies he wants to, since comic book movie
fans always flock to larger theaters and make

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:12.020
the filmgoing experience unenjoyable for him.

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:19.500
"Now I gotta go travel 15, 20 minutes to a
smaller movie theater to see a grown-up movie

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:20.860
with other grown-ups?"

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.920
O'Brien then laughed when asking whether Maron
intended to come on the show and alienate

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:28.900
a ton of people, which prompted Maron to say
that he may have overdone it a little bit.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:30.580
"I, you know, look, I just don't go see them.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:31.520
I'm not interested."

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:32.140
"Right."

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:32.780
"That's all."

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.820
That wasn't enough to stop Marvel loyals from
going after Maron on social media.

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:41.120
It wasn't long before the actor-comedian again
addressed angry fans this time taking things

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:42.260
a few steps further.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:43.180
Maron tweeted,

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:44.900
"Hey, Marvel movie fans!

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:48.300
Stop acting like outraged religious fanatics
defending their belief system.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:49.740
It's okay if I don't believe.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:50.500
Let it go.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:53.460
Also, I'm actually [a] big fan of a lot of
comic art.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.360
Try to relax your mainstream asses."

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:56.650
He added in another tweet,

00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:59.580
"good times doing the troll dance with emotional
baby brains.

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:01.880
forgot what an exciting waste of time this
can be."

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:05.920
Anyone familiar with Maron will know that
this opinion of his didn't spring out of nowhere.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:10.240
He's long maintained status as a comic book
movie opposer, previously stating during an

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:12.980
episode of his podcast WTF with Marc Maron,

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:17.020
"[If] I seem slightly condescending to superhero
movies and you think that's rude, I want to

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:20.700
tell you this, honestly and from the heart:
I will continue to do it.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:25.080
I will continue to condescend to grown-ups
who defend, almost maniacally, the integrity

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.320
and need and greatness of superhero movies."

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:31.540
Maron also condemned comic book movies for
pushing aside what he calls "real dialogue

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:35.600
and real human stories" to the point that
he feels there are very few movies left being

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:40.190
made that are, quote, "provocative and proactive
in terms of making you think and making you

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:42.940
move forward with your life and seeing things
differently."

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:46.580
What's interesting about Maron's remarks is
the fact that he himself is in a comic book

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:47.080
movie.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:51.280
Granted, the Todd Phillips-directed, Joaquin
Phoenix-starring Joker doesn't outwardly appear

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:55.870
like your average comic book adaptation it's
darker, eerier, and evidently tells a very

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:58.300
different tale of DC's Clown Prince of Crime.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:02.580
It appears that Maron eased up on his stance
with Joker for that reason plus the fact that

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:05.870
starring in the film means that he got to
work with Phoenix and Robert De Niro, who

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:07.920
plays talk show host Murray Franklin.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:12.300
Maron went on record in the past to praise
Phillips' vision and affirm that Joker isn't

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:13.760
like other comic book films.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.040
Maron told NME in March 2019,

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:19.620
"I've been somewhat judgmental when it comes
to comic book movies and I've got a little

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:23.800
pushback in the press for being a hypocrite…Oddly,
[Joker is] not that kind of movie.

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:27.380
The approach that Todd Phillips has taken
is more of an origin story and a character

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:30.280
study of a mentally ill person that becomes
the Joker.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:33.500
It's more of an intimate and gritty movie
with a very specific scope.

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:36.400
It's going to be really interesting to see
how it comes out."

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.740
Superhero films aren't everyone's cup of tea.

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:42.340
It's best to live and let live…and prepare
for what's apparently going to be a comic

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:46.760
book movie unlike anything you've seen before
when Joker hits theaters on October 4th.

